88405df9aa92944f5f6d62a35", "bytes": 227226, "lines": 531, "events_no_deltas": [{"type": "system", "subtype": "init", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "tools": ["StructuredOutput"], "mcp_servers": [], "permissionMode": "auto", "claude_code_version": "2.1.294", "output_style": "default", "init_sha256": "19a6ffcf0781096cd8fadcc901d1f698c81748761870f4f438dc6f07a56b3d9a"}, {"type": "system", "subtype": "status", "status": "requesting"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "message_start", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgQYYrZvXkmgpkkwmiVSX", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 355, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5754, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 355}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "ttft_ms": 2486, "thinking_display": "updates"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 0, "content_block": {"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "thinking_display": "updates"}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgQYYrZvXkmgpkkwmiVSX", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": {"длина": 43028, "sha256": "b5923fea685080bfcf1729d5e27b87bd3b41c77fabaa07425b2aa68da507d5c4"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 355, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5754, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 355}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T08:39:52.946Z", "request_id": "req_011CgQYYrKJYgpTkiBMTjUDQ", "thinking_duration_ms": 154022}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 0}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 1, "content_block": {"type": "text", "text": ""}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgQYYrZvXkmgpkkwmiVSX", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I picked **Candidate 0**. I worked the numbers in my head with an approximate model, not a full day-by-day simulation, so this is a best estimate. Cand 0 comes out ahead of the next best, Cand 3, by about 500, and of Cand 4 by about 330.\n\n**How the candidates are built:**\n- **Cand 0:** orders every 2 days, and each order equals the forecast demand for the days it covers. For example, 41 = 21 + 20 and 74 = 31 + 43. Over the whole plan it orders about 4.6 % less than true average demand (forecast × 1.046).\n- **Cand 1, 2, 3, 5:** the same schedule scaled up. Cand 1 is about ×1.10, Cand 2 about ×1.15 (its last two orders drop back to forecast), Cand 3 is ×1.15 for product 0 and ×1.05 for product 1, and Cand 5 is about ×1.25.\n- **Cand 4 and 7:** order every 3 days. Cand 4 orders at forecast level, Cand 7 about 10 % above.\n- **Cand 6:** orders every day, which costs 28 × 38 = 1064 in order fees against 532 for the every-2-days plans.\n\n**Main trade-off.** Stock lasts 8 days, so units left over carry into later days and rarely spoil. That means \"ordered more than demand\" and \"ran short\" add up over the 30 days like a random walk. Each extra unit costs 6–7 to buy and is only worth 15 (sale plus avoided penalty) if it actually prevents a shortage. So it needs to prevent one about 40–47 % of the time. On top of that, the surplus sits in stock and is charged storage every day until the end, and whatever is left on day 29 is lost.\n\nI estimated expected shortages with the standard random-walk formula (Brownian motion with drift). The spread of total demand over the horizon is about 52 units for product 0 and about 65 for product 1. Totals for both products (relative values, higher is better):\n\n| Plan | Lost sales 0 / 1 | Left at end 0 / 1 | Total |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Cand 0 | ~63 / ~83 | ~26 / ~31 | ≈ −14 900 |\n| Cand 1 | ~24 / ~29 | ~69 / ~90 | ≈ −15 300 |\n| Cand 3 | ~16 / ~49 | ~100 / ~55 | ≈ −15 400 |\n| Cand 2 | ~18 / ~21 | ~87 / ~114 | ≈ −15 750 |\n| Cand 5 | lowest shortages | about 220 left of product 1 alone | clearly worse |\n\nThe bigger orders do cut shortages. But the extra purchases, the extra stock left at the end and the daily storage on the growing surplus cost more than the shortages they save.\n\n**The other schedules:**\n- **Cand 4:** saves 152 in order fees, but holding a 3-day supply costs about 350 more in storage. It also orders less product 1 than forecast, for example 100 instead of 116 on day 18, and around days 21–23 stock gets close to the 224-unit limit. Net, it is about 330 worse than Cand 0.\n- **Cand 7:** the same schedule as Cand 4 with more stock, so it is worse still.\n- **Cand 6:** ordering daily saves about 350 in storage but pays 532 more in order fees, and it orders about 10 % above forecast.\n\n**If demand differs from the forecast:** the starting shortage on days 0–2 is the same for every plan. After that, the bigger plans only gain when demand comes in well above forecast. When demand is normal or low, they lose through leftover stock and storage. Cand 0's losses are smaller and less sensitive to how demand turns out."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 355, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5754, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 355}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T08:40:05.992Z", "request_id": "req_011CgQYYrKJYgpTkiBMTjUDQ"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01E6t8LVbHoMWJZq4arX7EkP", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgQYYrZvXkmgpkkwmiVSX", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01E6t8LVbHoMWJZq4arX7EkP", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {"choice": 0}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 355, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5754, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 355}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T08:40:06.221Z", "request_id": "req_011CgQYYrKJYgpTkiBMTjUDQ"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 2}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01E6t8LVbHoMWJZq4arX7EkP", "type": "tool_result", "content": "Structured output provided successfully"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T08:40:06.238Z", "tool_use_result": "Structured out